# Everything that must run after tools has defined its widgets.

# -- Key bindings
# Force the emacs keymap. zsh would otherwise pick viins, because $EDITOR
# matches *vi* -- this, not `bindkey -v`, is why vi-mode kept coming back.
bindkey -e

# ctrl+left / ctrl+right in Ghostty send ^[b / ^[f (see ghostty.config).
# These restate emacs defaults, deliberately: they survive a plugin that
# rebinds them later, and they document the intent.
# emacs-forward-word, not forward-word: the latter moves to the *beginning of
# the next* word, the former to the *end of the current* one -- which is what
# readline does in every other program on this machine.
bindkey '^[b' backward-word
bindkey '^[f' emacs-forward-word

bindkey '^A' beginning-of-line
bindkey '^E' end-of-line

# ^X^E opens the current line in $EDITOR -- nvim, with NVIM_APPNAME=lazyvim
# (see env). Unlike bash's ^X^E this does not run the command on save: the
# edited text comes back to the prompt and you press Enter yourself.
# Must precede zsh-syntax-highlighting, which wraps every widget it finds.
autoload -Uz edit-command-line
zle -N edit-command-line
bindkey '^X^E' edit-command-line

# Tab is fzf's fuzzy completion.
#
# The -M emacs is load-bearing, and the reason this was broken for a while:
# fzf's setup ends with a bare `bindkey '^I' fzf-completion`, and a bare
# bindkey lands in whatever keymap is current -- viins, because zsh picks the
# default keymap from $EDITOR and that matches *vi* (see env). Drop the -M
# emacs and fzf's Tab becomes reachable only in vi mode, while this shell
# silently falls back to zsh's expand-or-complete.
#
# ROLLBACK: for zsh's own completion instead, swap the line below for
#   bindkey -M emacs '^I' expand-or-complete
bindkey -M emacs '^I' fzf-completion

# Do NOT bind ^R here. fzf owns it and binds it with -M emacs explicitly, so a
# manual bindkey would silently shadow fzf-history-widget.
# ^T is not in that list: Ghostty binds it to new_tab (see ghostty.config), so
# the key never reaches zsh and fzf-file-widget is unreachable by design.

# -- Syntax highlighting
# Must come after every widget it needs to wrap. Upstream README: source last.
source "$HOMEBREW_PREFIX/share/zsh-syntax-highlighting/zsh-syntax-highlighting.zsh"

# -- Prompt
eval "$(starship init zsh)"
